# Personal working notes — raw voice transcripts. The repo goes public before
# the demo (PRD §16), so these stay local.
docs/Rec.txt
docs/Rec2.txt

# Beads — issues.jsonl is the git-tracked source of truth; the db is not
.beads/*.db
.beads/*.db-*

# Kona runtime state — a pursuit's .kona/ never belongs in the repo (spec §6.1)
.kona/

# Toolchain
node_modules/
dist/
*.log

# Stryker sandboxes and reports
.stryker-tmp/
reports/

# Other windows' worktrees of this same repo
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-epic working notes from the parallel windows. Local scratch, not a deliverable —
# whatever they settled that still matters is in the spec, the tests or a beads issue.
plans/

# The evidence base stays private. Both directories quote heavily from primary sources —
# vendor docs, papers, issue threads — and the probe transcripts carry raw model output from
# runs that were never written to be read by anyone but us. The CONCLUSIONS are public: every
# claim they support is stated, with its measurement, in prd.md / spec.md / plan.md and in the
# code comments at the decisions they justify.
docs/probes/
docs/research/
